BULL BLOCKED (link#227) — 7 blocking dam(s) on BULL's downstream flow path have not been modelled yet.

link computes accessibility by reading ALREADY-PERSISTED downstream barriers.
Running BULL now would mark segments accessible that are in fact dammed off, and exit 0.

  persist schema : fresh_default
  unmodelled blocking dams downstream of BULL:
    KOTL  1d905323-2558-493d-8481-8679dfe79b01   Brilliant Dam (psc 1)
    KOTL  8745c255-2288-417c-96ef-6dbadf302ee5   Corra Linn Dam (psc 1)
    KOTL  85d7371b-2d13-4749-ad55-a93bbefcbf40   Lower Bonnington Dam (psc 1)
    KOTL  e9304187-0916-472d-88b4-de53d5c4076a   South Slocan Dam (psc 1)
    KOTL  664978eb-9916-47cd-9e9b-c1094d55b5cd   South Slocan Generating Station (psc 1)
    KOTL  7cf09664-f257-41e3-9db3-728e3b939b4e   Upper Bonnington Dam (psc 1)
    LARL  1200000002                             Grand Coulee Dam (psc 1)
  model these first, DS-first: LARL, KOTL

Fix — pick one:
  1. Model the downstream WSGs first:
       for w in LARL KOTL; do Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R $w <config>; done
  2. Model BULL now and settle access after they land:
       Rscript data-raw/wsg_recompute_one.R BULL <config>
  3. Override, if those dams are known passable / remediated / irrelevant.
     Recorded in the run log and surfaced by lnk_log_read():
       LNK_GUARD_DOWNSTREAM_NOTE="..." Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R BULL <config>

