COLR BLOCKED (link#227) — 3 blocking dam(s) on COLR's downstream flow path have not been modelled yet.

link computes accessibility by reading ALREADY-PERSISTED downstream barriers.
Running COLR now would mark segments accessible that are in fact dammed off, and exit 0.

  persist schema : fresh_default
  unmodelled blocking dams downstream of COLR:
    LARL  1200000002                             Grand Coulee Dam (psc 1)
    LARL  aac817e2-9175-4d8c-8b9a-10177622fc62   Hugh Keenleyside Dam (psc 1)
    REVL  65d93eb9-55ae-4b1d-9d1b-7c1480ea50ac   Revelstoke Dam (psc 1)
  model these first, DS-first: LARL, UARL, REVL, CLRH, CANO, KHOR

Fix — pick one:
  1. Model the downstream WSGs first:
       for w in LARL UARL REVL CLRH CANO KHOR; do Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R $w <config>; done
  2. Model COLR now and settle access after they land:
       Rscript data-raw/wsg_recompute_one.R COLR <config>
  3. Override, if those dams are known passable / remediated / irrelevant.
     Recorded in the run log and surfaced by lnk_log_read():
       LNK_GUARD_DOWNSTREAM_NOTE="..." Rscript data-raw/wsg_run_one.R COLR <config>

